$NetBSD$

Do not insist on a separate libdl.

meson.build has

	# Checks for libdl - on certain platforms its part of libc
	dl_dep = cc.find_library('dl')

with no required: false, so configure stops on any system where dlopen()
lives in libc rather than in its own library:

	meson.build:330:12: ERROR: C shared or static library 'dl' not found

That is every BSD.  The comment above the line says as much, and the
lines that follow it are the portable version -- walking find_library,
then dependency('dl'), then dependency('dld') -- except that they sit
inside a ''' ... ''' string and never run.  Both 1.50.0 and 1.58.1 carry
it that way.

src/core/meson.build puts dl_dep straight into the nm_deps list, so a
not-found dependency would not do; declare_dependency() gives an empty
one that the list accepts.

--- meson.build.orig
+++ meson.build
@@ -327,7 +327,13 @@
 config_h.set10('HAVE_WEXT', enable_wext)
 
 # Checks for libdl - on certain platforms its part of libc
-dl_dep = cc.find_library('dl')
+dl_dep = cc.find_library('dl', required: false)
+if not dl_dep.found()
+  # dlopen() and friends live in libc on the BSDs, so there is no separate
+  # library to find.  nm_deps in src/core/meson.build takes dl_dep by value,
+  # so hand it an empty dependency rather than a not-found one.
+  dl_dep = declare_dependency()
+endif
 '''
 dl_deps = []
 
